{"slug":"ops-prod-ops","title":"Production operations","blocks":[{"id":"b1","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Production environment (canonical)"},{"id":"b2","type":"table","head":[[{"type":"text","value":"Fact"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Value"}]],"rows":[[[{"type":"text","value":"Host"}],[{"type":"text","value":"89.167.28.206","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — Hetzner cax11, ARM64 (aarch64), Ubuntu 22.04"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"App dir"}],[{"type":"text","value":"/opt/barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (server tracks "},{"type":"text","value":"origin/main","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"core.hooksPath=.githooks","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Service"}],[{"type":"text","value":"systemd "},{"type":"text","value":"barkpark.service","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; wrapper "},{"type":"text","value":"api/start.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (sources ASDF + "},{"type":"text","value":".env","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Proxy"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Caddy on :80 → "},{"type":"text","value":"localhost:4000","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"text","value":"/etc/caddy/Caddyfile","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Erlang/Elixir"}],[{"type":"text","value":"via ASDF (Erlang Solutions has no ARM packages)"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Go"}],[{"type":"text","value":"/usr/local/go/bin/go","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (official ARM64 binary)"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Env file"}],[{"type":"text","value":"/opt/barkpark/.env","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"text","value":"DATABASE_URL","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"SECRET_KEY_BASE","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"BARKPARK_EXTRA_ORIGINS","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ws origins)"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Logs"}],[{"type":"text","value":"journalctl -u barkpark -f","marks":["code"]}]]]},{"id":"b3","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Deploy: "},{"type":"text","value":"ssh root@89.167.28.206","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", then on the box "},{"type":"text","value":"cd /opt/barkpark && git pull","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (the post-merge hook rebuilds + restarts; "},{"type":"text","value":"make deploy","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" wraps it). Golden Rules 2/3/6 apply ("},{"type":"text","value":"CLAUDE.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"id":"b4","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The toolchain pin is a production change.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" The box's asdf resolves repo-root "},{"type":"text","value":".tool-versions","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"text","value":"/opt/barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (the running BEAM reports elixir 1.18.4-otp-27 / erts-15.2.7), so editing it moves prod — never in a PR that changes anything else. "},{"type":"text","value":"elixir.yml","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"'s "},{"type":"text","value":"mix-prod-compile","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"text","value":"mix-test","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" matrices carry the same 1.18.4, so a green prod-compile means \"compiles on the box\"; they pin "},{"type":"text","value":"otp: \"27.0\"","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" below the box's 27.3.4 on purpose (wider blast radius)."}]},{"id":"b5","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The postcheck rule"},{"id":"b6","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A misbooted or stopped node looks identical to a healthy one from outside, so any workflow touching "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on prod "},{"type":"text","value":"must","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" end with "},{"type":"text","value":"api/scripts/prod-postcheck.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and confirm "},{"type":"text","value":"PASS prod healthy …","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Prefer "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl restart","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" to stop-then-start (document a deliberate stop), and a make target ("},{"type":"text","value":"make deploy","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"text","value":"rebuild","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"text","value":"restart","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") to ad-hoc "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":"b7","type":"code","language":"bash","value":"ssh root@<prod-host> \"cd /opt/barkpark && ./api/scripts/prod-postcheck.sh\"\n# QUOTED, or the cd runs on your laptop. On the box: drop the ssh wrapper."},{"id":"b8","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Exit 0 = healthy; non-zero writes a "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl status","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" tail to stderr. It checks service active (if inactive it STARTS it — a guardrail, not a monitor), a 2 s delay to bind "},{"type":"text","value":":4000","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", and HTTP 200 from "},{"type":"text","value":"/api/schemas","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (unauth JSON; swap to "},{"type":"text","value":"/studio","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" if retired, never the admin-gated "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/schemas/production","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"). On FAIL read that tail, then "},{"type":"text","value":"journalctl -u barkpark -n 200 --no-pager","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — never retry blindly. After a deploy tail "},{"type":"text","value":"journalctl -u barkpark -f","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" >=60 s for boot errors, supervisor restart loops and 5xx."}]},{"id":"b9","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Operator one-shots (live box)"},{"id":"b10","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"mix barkpark.*","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" one-shots boot the Repo + their own deps only ("},{"type":"text","value":"Barkpark.MixBoot","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") — never the Endpoint, Oban, plugin workers or the codelist seeders, so an inherited "},{"type":"text","value":"PHX_SERVER","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" binds nothing. Fix for guerrilla 2026-09-02 ("},{"type":"text","value":"barkpark.edges.backfill","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":": dry-run 08:32:41Z, apply 08:34:58Z, +1260/-1199 edges), where "},{"type":"text","value":"app.start","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" bound :4001 against the live node, started a second Oban on the live queues, and timed a codelist seed out. Run them cool anyway:"}]},{"id":"b11","type":"code","language":"bash","value":"ssh root@89.167.28.206; cd /opt/barkpark/api\n. \"$HOME/.asdf/asdf.sh\"               # same toolchain init as api/start.sh\nset -a; . /opt/barkpark/.env; set +a  # env SOURCE: the slot's .env, not yours\nMIX_ENV=prod MIX_BUILD_ROOT=<active slot build root> nice -n 19 \\\n  mix barkpark.edges.backfill         # dry run; --apply writes"},{"id":"b12","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"MIX_BUILD_ROOT","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" at the ACTIVE slot's build root reuses the warm build (a cold compile took load 1.9 → 6.3 on this 2-core box); "},{"type":"text","value":"nice -n 19","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" keeps the sweep behind live traffic."}]},{"id":"b13","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Prod migrations — validated live 2026-06-10"},{"id":"b14","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook DOES migrate: "},{"type":"text","value":"deploy-rebuild.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" runs "},{"type":"text","value":"ecto.migrate","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on new code while the old build serves, aborting the swap on failure (exit 13). By hand keep that order — new code selecting an unmigrated column 500s every request:"}]},{"id":"b15","type":"code","language":"bash","value":"ssh root@89.167.28.206   # then ON THE BOX — never `&&`, that cd's on your laptop\ncd /opt/barkpark\nset -a; . ./.env; set +a                    # backup: ecto:// -> postgresql://\npg_dump \"${DATABASE_URL/ecto:/postgresql:}\" | gzip > /root/pre-deploy.sql.gz\ngit checkout -- bin/barkpark bin/barkpark-pg go.sum  # dirtied artifacts abort the pull\ngit -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null pull --ff-only  # NO hook — old code keeps serving\nmake migrate               # start.sh mix ecto.migrate (ASDF + .env)\nbash .githooks/post-merge  # rebuild + migrate + restart — SEE WARNING BELOW\n./api/scripts/prod-postcheck.sh"},{"id":"b16","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Destructive migrations (drop/rename) have no zero-downtime order — schedule a window: stop, migrate, deploy, start. Never "},{"type":"text","value":"make reset-db","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"text","value":"mix ecto.reset","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on prod; a migration that fails mid-way is stop-and-forward-fix, never an edit to an applied one."}]},{"id":"b17","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook cannot report failure.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" It exits 0 even when the rebuild fails (old build keeps serving), so "},{"type":"text","value":"prod-postcheck.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" PASSes against that old build: grep its output for "},{"type":"text","value":"WARN: deploy-rebuild failed","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". A green postcheck proves the service is up, never that your code deployed; a no-op on "},{"type":"text","value":".slots","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" boxes."}]},{"id":"b18","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Phoenix server rollback"},{"id":"b19","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Revert source; never reset the server checkout. On a BRANCH (main refuses a direct push — GH006 is correct) "},{"type":"text","value":"git revert <bad-sha>","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", push, merge via "},{"type":"text","value":"scripts/bp-merge.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; then on the box "},{"type":"text","value":"cd /opt/barkpark && git pull","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (the hook rebuilds + restarts) and run the postcheck. Never "},{"type":"text","value":"git reset --hard","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" or force-push the prod checkout; rebuild only via "},{"type":"text","value":"make rebuild","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (aside into "},{"type":"text","value":"api/_build_next","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", swaps on success), never a hand-rolled partial clean — that serves stale BEAM/HEEx (Past Mistakes #1-3). Rolling back code does NOT undo a schema change; write a compensating migration."}]},{"id":"b20","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Code anchors"},{"id":"b21","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"api/scripts/prod-postcheck.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — the postcheck script"}],[{"type":"text","value":".githooks/post-merge","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — rebuild + migrate + restart on server "},{"type":"text","value":"git pull","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Makefile","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — "},{"type":"text","value":"rebuild","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"text","value":"deploy","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"text","value":"migrate","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"text","value":"restart","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" targets"}],[{"type":"text","value":"api/start.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — systemd wrapper sourcing ASDF + "},{"type":"text","value":".env","marks":["code"]}]]}],"related":["ops-npm-rollback-playbook"]}
